from pathlib import Path
import json,html,base64
R=Path('/Users/sky/Projects/suborned');O=R/'out/scratch/codex/asset-quality-review';D=json.loads((O/'audit.json').read_text());e=html.escape
findings=[
('1','High','Give the civic façades the surface quality already present elsewhere',
 'CafeBay has 0 textured materials out of 9; CafeBay_v2 has 0/10 and CafeTerrace 0/7. DK_Limestone, the general enamel colours, cloth and chrome are largely constant-value materials. The current café shots show large clean panels with little material variation, beside textured paving and furniture.',
 'Add restrained stone grain, enamel roughness variation, cloth weave and contact detail to the café and Records Office first. Keep the palette, clean finish and brass hairlines. Use shared metric detail or trim sheets rather than a unique large atlas for every bay. Preserve edge highlights and deepen selected reveals where they improve the silhouette.',
 'The procedural district is a separate case: FacadeSurface.hlsl already implements limestone courses/grain, enamel grids, AO, bump and material classes. Extend and reconcile that work with the kit; a claim that all façades lack detail would be wrong.',
 [('unity/Assets/Suborned/Editor/World/Atlas.cs',38),('unity/Assets/Suborned/Shaders/FacadeSurface.hlsl',23),('tools/decokit/mats.py',30)]),
('2','High','Bring civic planting up to the palms’ standard',
 'The café’s hedge bands visibly read as repeated green domes and separate flower lumps. civic_common.py constructs those forms explicitly. The street palms use textured, bent foliage with authored normals and LODs, so the two approaches look like different quality tiers in the same shot.',
 'Keep the existing massing and clear planting boundaries, but give near hedge bands a leafy surface and a less regular outline. Test shared leaf-cluster textures/cards or restrained detail shading, subtle per-instance variation and better soil-to-planter contact. Retain simple distant masses.',
 'This needs an art comparison at the real tactical size. More leaf cards can increase overdraw; the goal is a cohesive look, not maximum foliage density.',
 [('tools/decokit/civic_common.py',75),('tools/decokit/civic_common.py',102),('tools/decokit/palm_lod.py',1)]),
('3','High','Restore selective character surface response without reintroducing wet cloth',
 'The installed cell uses Generic overrides. For Scout, Tech and Enforcer, cell_generic.py keeps albedo, normals and emission but drops ORM and sets body smoothness to 0.15; the visor is 0.75. Fixer keeps materials from the other build. The ordinary character pipeline also removes normals and metallic/AO/smoothness maps at its 512 tier. These are deliberate readability fixes, but they erase distinctions between cloth, skin, boots and trim.',
 'Author a controlled material mask for the close tier: matte cloth, softer skin highlights, distinct leather, and metal only on actual trim. Keep the stable tactical tier until an A/B proves a benefit. Use the source normal detail selectively and fix baked highlights in albedo rather than compensating for them with one global matte value.',
 'The old manifest does not describe the cell’s effective geometry: Scout is 29,148/12,000/4,500 triangles; Tech 33,628/14,999/6,999; Enforcer has one 28,796-triangle level. New Vale C work exists but is not represented by the installed manifest reviewed here; recheck after import.',
 [('tools/figures/cell_generic.py',196),('tools/figures/cell_generic.py',282),('tools/figures/build.py',333),('unity/Assets/Suborned/Editor/World/People/FigureBuild.cs',38)]),
('4','Medium','Improve hero reflections and glazing selectively',
 'Two 128 px HDR, box-projected baked probes already cover the civic square and Office front. Outside them the fallback is a generated 64 px RGBA32 cubemap: limited detail and no HDR highlight range. DK_GlassDark and procedural façade glass intentionally use synthetic sky/street reflections, which cannot reflect local architecture.',
 'Compare a 256 px baked hero probe and an HDR, specular-prefiltered fallback against today’s chrome posts, car trim and robot shells. For close glazing, test a local reflection blended with the existing stylized treatment. Keep the inexpensive district treatment where it reads well.',
 'These are quality experiments, not proof that the existing probes are broken. Realtime reflection probes across the district would be a poor first investment. Unity documents the existing box-projection and HDR probe controls.',
 [('unity/Assets/Suborned/Editor/World/Light/Probes.cs',28),('unity/Assets/Suborned/Editor/World/Proc/ReflectionCube.cs',28),('unity/Assets/Suborned/Shaders/DecoKit/DK_GlassSky.shader',1)]),
('5','Medium','Stop adding avoidable texture loss; make resolution exceptions evidence-based',
 'build.py re-encodes many opaque albedo and normal sources as JPEG quality 90. There are 37 installed character normal JPEGs; some originate as JPEG, so the extension alone is not a defect. The kit importer caps all kit textures at 2048, including five 4096 source maps. FBX export rounds UVs to 0.001 on bevelled models and distance versions.',
 'Preserve lossless source normal maps and let Unity perform platform compression. Inspect the pavilion and civic paving at their closest supported distance before allowing any 4096 exception. For atlas-mapped pieces, verify UV precision and padding: rounding can move an atlas coordinate by up to about one texel at 2K or two at 4K. Keep deterministic export, but choose precision for the actual texture density.',
 'This is confirmed pipeline loss/risk, not a measured visible failure on every asset. The 2K cap and streaming already save useful memory; global 4K imports would not solve flat shading.',
 [('tools/figures/build.py',83),('unity/Assets/Suborned/Editor/World/Kit/TextureBudget.cs',17),('tools/decokit/export_kit.py',129)]),
('6','Medium','Recover headroom from repeated geometry and material slots',
 '177 of 262 adopted catalogue assets have distance meshes; 85 do not. Some are intentionally tiny or flat. More useful follow-ups are DrainGrate (4,068 triangles × 50 exported placements), ManholeCover (5,388 × 16), BikeRack (7,572 × 10), and the 41,888-triangle fountain with no lower mesh. RobotWaiter has 18 material names, RobotShopkeeper 20, and the café interior 23.',
 'Profile repeated small props and material/submesh overhead first. Trial shared trim/packed masks and simplified distant grates, racks and covers while retaining their near silhouettes. Give the fountain and Enforcer appropriate far tiers if profiling justifies it. Evaluate selective LOD crossfades on visible transitions; kit groups currently switch without fading.',
 'These counts are opportunity indicators, not measured GPU costs. Export placements are district-wide, not simultaneously visible objects. Do not compress approved models automatically; preserve the repository’s model-quality sign-off process. Clear coat is useful for enamel but adds lighting cost.',
 [('unity/Assets/Suborned/Editor/World/Kit/KitLods.cs',163),('tools/kit/lod.ts',1),('contracts/world/kit.json',1)]),
('7','Medium','Judge the final look through the game’s presentation effects',
 'The saved build 0.2.117 images still show a conspicuous stippled façade veil over the café, and night grading greatly reduces surface and character separation. These effects can hide good modelling and texture work. ArchitectureFade and the cutaway shader deliberately create the veil; lens and light-phase code already contain newer night adjustments.',
 'Review assets both with their normal gameplay presentation and in a neutral comparison. Keep the cutaway’s gameplay purpose, then tune the veil and night material separation using the newest build. Require day, dusk and night examples of the same stone, enamel, chrome, foliage and skin.',
 'The supplied game captures are evidence from build 0.2.117, not a fresh render of every uncommitted change. I have not labelled already-addressed night work as a current regression.',
 [('unity/Assets/Suborned/Shaders/DecoKit/DK_Cutaway.hlsl',50),('unity/Assets/Suborned/Runtime/AtmosphereLens.cs',91),('unity/Assets/Suborned/Resources/Atmosphere/lens.json',1)])]

style='''body{margin:0;color:#dce5e9;background:#11191d;font:15px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:36px 24px}h1,h2,h3{line-height:1.2;color:#f5f6f4}h1{font-size:34px;margin-bottom:10px}h2{margin-top:40px;font-size:25px}h3{font-size:20px;margin:8px 0 16px}a{color:#86d9d0}p{max-width:95ch}.muted,small{color:#a7b5be}.lead{font-size:19px}.stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px;margin:24px 0}.stats div,.finding{border:1px solid #33434a;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;background:#18242a}.stats b{display:block;font-size:27px;color:#95dfd0}.finding{margin:16px 0}.tag{display:inline-block;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;color:#f2cf91}.evidence{font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px}figure{margin:0}img{width:100%;display:block;border-radius:8px}figcaption{color:#b6c2c8;font-size:13px;padding:8px 0}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px}th,td{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #33434a;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{color:#a0ddd3}input,select{font:inherit;padding:9px;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #587078;color:#dce5e9;background:#18242a}input{width:310px;max-width:95%}.scroll{overflow:auto;max-height:650px}details{border:1px solid #33434a;border-radius:9px;padding:16px;margin:16px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;color:#b3e0d8;font-weight:600}code{font-size:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.check{color:#a9dfb8}@media(max-width:650px){main{padding:22px 14px}.stats{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:28px}}'''
def picture(path,caption):
 p=R/path;mime='image/png' if p.suffix=='.png' else 'image/jpeg';src='data:'+mime+';base64,'+base64.b64encode(p.read_bytes()).decode();return f'<figure><img src="{src}" alt="{e(caption)}"><figcaption>{e(caption)}</figcaption></figure>'
rows=[]
for x in D['kit']:
 rows.append({'id':x['id'],'category':x['category'],'status':x['status'],'tris':x['tris'],'lods':' / '.join(str(l['tris']) for l in x.get('lods',[])) or 'None','materials':len(x.get('materials',[])),'textured':x['texturedMaterials'],'normals':x['normalMaterials'],'placed':x['exportPlacements']})
char=[]
for f in D['figures']:
 a=f.get('effectiveOverride',f);char.append({'id':f['id'],'build':'Generic override' if 'effectiveOverride' in f else 'Humanoid','triangles':' / '.join(str(l['tris']) for l in a['lods']),'maps':', '.join(sorted(set(t for m in a['materials'] for t in m.get('textures',{}))))})
head=f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The Suborned — model and material quality review</title><style>{style}</style><main>'
parts=[head,'<small>25 October 2026 · Read-only review · Unity 6000.6.2f1 / URP 17.6</small><h1>There is substantial visual headroom.</h1><p class="lead">The strongest next step is a coordinated material and foliage pass on the civic block. The underlying asset and import pipeline is healthy; inconsistent surface treatment is the main limit on the look.</p>',
'<div class="stats"><div><b>347</b>catalogue entries<br><small>262 adopted · 77 candidate · 8 rejected</small></div><div><b>612</b>FBXs containing geometry<br><small>588 kit · 23 figures + 1 tray</small></div><div><b>288</b>kit + people materials<br><small>217 kit · 71 people</small></div><div><b>225</b>kit + people image textures<br><small>88 kit · 137 people</small></div></div>',
'<p><b>Scope:</b> audited every installed kit and people FBX, every catalogue row, all 288 kit/people material files and their texture references, all 225 image texture imports, procedural façade shading, render settings, source exporters and character overrides. The other 65 people FBXs are animation-only. Reviewed representative saved game images and family boards; this is not a new turntable render of every asset. Sixteen additional loose scene, signal and test materials were inventoried separately.</p>',
'<p class="check"><b>Healthy checks:</b> all 677 FBXs parsed; no non-finite vertex/normal/UV values; no missing mesh normals; all tested material texture references resolve; bound normal, mask and detail maps have the expected shader keywords. Normal maps and packed masks have the expected colour-space/type flags. The tray has no UVs and uses untextured materials, which is appropriate. Every adopted primary FBX found by path matches the catalogue triangle count.</p>',
'<p><b>Already working well:</b> weighted normals and bevel support, Mikk tangents, correct packed metallic/AO/smoothness channels, foliage alpha-coverage mipmaps, trilinear/anisotropic filtering, 2K texture budgeting, streaming, HDR rendering, SMAA on the host camera, SSAO, SRP Batcher/GPU Resident Drawer, two baked HDR reflection probes, and authored palm LODs. Preserve these foundations.</p>',
'<h2>The visible quality gap</h2><div class="grid">',picture('out/batch/shots/cafe-front-day.png','Game build 0.2.117: detailed paving and furniture beside flatter façade panels and repeated civic hedge forms.'),picture('out/batch/shots/follow-scout-cafe.png','Same saved build, follow camera: this is where cloth, stone, enamel, metal and glazing need distinct responses.'),'</div>',
'<h2>Ranked findings</h2>']
for no,priority,title,obs,action,qual,sources in findings:
 refs=' · '.join(f'<a href="{e(str(R/p))}">{e(p)}:{ln}</a>' for p,ln in sources)
 parts.append(f'<article class="finding"><span class="tag">{priority} priority · {no}</span><h3>{e(title)}</h3><p><b>Evidence.</b> {e(obs)}</p><p><b>Recommended change.</b> {e(action)}</p><p class="muted">{e(qual)}</p><p class="evidence">{refs}</p></article>')
parts+=['<h2>Where to spend effort by family</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Family</th><th>Assessment</th><th>Best next investment</th></tr></thead><tbody>',
'<tr><td>Buildings / façades</td><td>Strong forms; kit and procedural paths differ in richness.</td><td>Café and Office shared detail, reveals, consistent stone/enamel treatment.</td></tr><tr><td>Plants</td><td>Palms are much richer than civic hedge bands.</td><td>Near hedge silhouette and leaf treatment; preserve tactical clarity.</td></tr><tr><td>People</td><td>Good source detail; intentionally broad matte response and mixed pipelines.</td><td>Material masks for skin, cloth, boots and trim; verify Vale C after import.</td></tr><tr><td>Robots / furniture</td><td>Strong silhouettes and some detailed materials; many slots.</td><td>Keep near quality; consolidate small surfaces and profile distant variants.</td></tr><tr><td>Roads / paving</td><td>PBR, metric UVs and source detail are already present.</td><td>Control large-scale repetition and road sheen; selective atlas resolution checks.</td></tr><tr><td>Vehicles</td><td>Readable 3,408-triangle sedan silhouettes with 10 material names.</td><td>Close-view seam/trim definition and better glass/paint reflections before more polygons.</td></tr><tr><td>Signs / crossings</td><td>Broad/signature forms and emission have useful role clarity.</td><td>Check glyph and trim sharpness in the newest crossing build; avoid blowing away glyph edges with bloom.</td></tr><tr><td>Skyline / landmarks</td><td>Silhouette, haze and authored distance shapes matter most.</td><td>Review long shots for material/LOD transitions; spend texture memory on near landmarks first.</td></tr></tbody></table>',
'<h2>Recommended first pass</h2><ol><li>Make one matched comparison at the café: one bay, planter band, chrome post and a dressed character, at tactical and follow distances.</li><li>Use three controlled changes: façade surface detail, leaf treatment and character material masks. Keep lighting fixed for the comparison, then check the result in day, dusk and night.</li><li>Compare hero reflections and atlas precision/resolution separately so their value can be judged.</li><li>Check movement, four camera headings and LOD thresholds. Keep the gameplay cutaway active for final acceptance.</li><li>Measure the candidate on the 15-inch M4 MacBook Air. Require 60 fps at play zoom with a busy crowd/fight; include frame-time distribution, texture residency and draw/submesh counts. No new performance claim is made by this audit.</li></ol>',
'<h2>Complete catalogue inspection</h2><p>Filter all 347 entries below. “Textured” means any bound texture, including emission/detail; it is not a quality score. A constant material can be exactly right for chrome or a simple painted surface. Placement counts come from the exported district and exclude runtime-only actors.</p><p><input id="q" aria-label="Search asset id or category" placeholder="Search asset or category…"> <select id="status" aria-label="Filter status"><option value="">All statuses</option><option selected>adopted</option><option>candidate</option><option>rejected</option></select> <span id="count" class="muted"></span></p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Asset</th><th>Family / state</th><th>L0 triangles</th><th>Far triangles</th><th>Material names</th><th>Textured / normal-detail</th><th>Export placements</th></tr></thead><tbody id="kit"></tbody></table></div>',
'<details><summary>All 23 installed character families, with effective cell overrides</summary><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Figure</th><th>Pipeline</th><th>Triangles by level</th><th>Maps present across tiers</th></tr></thead><tbody>']
for f in char:parts.append('<tr>'+''.join(f'<td>{e(str(f[k]))}</td>' for k in ['id','build','triangles','maps'])+'</tr>')
parts+=['</tbody></table></div></details><details><summary>All 677 installed FBX files</summary><p>File-array inspection, before Unity’s importer. Geometry-free files are animation clips. Normals can be recalculated by Unity; imported runtime geometry was not inspected live.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Triangles</th><th>Meshes</th><th>UV / normals</th></tr></thead><tbody>']
for f in D['models']:
 parts.append(f'<tr><td><code>{e(f["path"])}</code></td><td>{f.get("tris",0):,}</td><td>{len(f.get("meshes",[]))}</td><td>{"animation-only" if not f.get("meshes") else ("untextured tray: no UV" if f.get("missingUV") else "present")}</td></tr>')
parts+=['</tbody></table></div></details>',
'<h2>Verification limits and references</h2><p>This review reads the working tree as found, including ongoing changes. It does not alter source assets, scenes, import settings, game code or the GDD. Outputs are confined to this scratch report folder. Saved main-game evidence is build 0.2.117; later unbuilt adjustments may differ. No paid model calls, new Unity build, GPU profile or Air run was started. The accompanying audit.json contains the detailed material, texture, geometry and catalogue inventory.</p>',
'<p>Technical references: <a href="https://docs.unity.com/en-us/engine/6000.5/manual/materials-and-shaders/built-in/shaders-in-universalrp/reference/shader-complex-lit">Unity Complex Lit controls and clear-coat cost</a>; <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/ReflectionProbe.html">Unity reflection-probe controls</a>; <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.1/Documentation/Manual/StandardShaderMaterialParameterNormalMap.html">Unity normal-map conventions</a>. The installed URP package shader source was also inspected to verify detail-normal handling.</p>',
'<script>const rows='+json.dumps(rows,separators=(',',':'))+''';const esc=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));function draw(){const q=document.getElementById('q').value.toLowerCase(),status=document.getElementById('status').value;const a=rows.filter(x=>(!status||x.status===status)&&(!q||(x.id+' '+x.category).toLowerCase().includes(q)));document.getElementById('count').textContent=a.length+' entries';document.getElementById('kit').innerHTML=a.map(x=>'<tr><td>'+esc(x.id)+'</td><td>'+esc(x.category)+'<br><small>'+esc(x.status)+'</small></td><td>'+x.tris.toLocaleString()+'</td><td>'+esc(x.lods)+'</td><td>'+x.materials+'</td><td>'+x.textured+' / '+x.normals+'</td><td>'+x.placed+'</td></tr>').join('')}document.getElementById('q').addEventListener('input',draw);document.getElementById('status').addEventListener('change',draw);draw();</script></main></html>''']
(O/'review.html').write_text(''.join(parts));print('Wrote review.html', (O/'review.html').stat().st_size)
